From: Bryan Roscoe <bryanroscoe@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:10:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 27/30] Mana: a land's "{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color"
 activates when chosen

Study Hall: "{T}: Add {C}. {1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color. When you
spend this mana to cast your commander, scry X, ..."

CR 605.3b + CR 601.2g + CR 117.1d: a player may activate mana abilities
while paying, and an any-color ability's color is chosen as it resolves.
The mana-source list offers a land's any-color ability as one selection
with a deferred color, but tapping a land checked the selection against
the per-color rows only, so it was refused as stale. The castability
check walks exactly that route (a Wastes for the {1}, then Study Hall),
so a spell such as {2}{W} with W only from Study Hall was never offered.
Tapping a land now accepts the deferred selection, as nonland sources
already do, and the ability asks for its color as it resolves. A
concrete selection still has to match exactly one live row.

Test: tests/integration/study_hall_costed_any_color_land.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
